			"y": 200,
			"width": 390,
			"height": 1190,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "light",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Light and the spectrum\nPhotons; visible 380–750 nm; shorter λ = more energy\n\n[[Light and the Electromagnetic Spectrum|open note]]",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "pig",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Pigments\nChlorophyll a (main), chlorophyll b and carotenoids (accessory); absorption vs. action spectrum\n\n[[Photosynthetic Pigments|open note]]",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 490,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "exc",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Excited chlorophyll\ne⁻ jumps up; caught by an acceptor, or falls back as heat + red light\n\n[[Chlorophyll Excitation and Fluorescence|open note]]",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "eff",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Energy efficiency\nReflected, transmitted, absorbed; only a few % stored in sugar\n\n[[Energy Efficiency of Photosynthesis|open note]]",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 950,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "act7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Activity 7\nExtract reflects green, glows red; pigments absorb different colors\n\n[[Activity 7 - Light and Pigments|open note]]",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 1180,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "chl",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Chloroplast\nThylakoid, granum, stroma, lumen\n\n[[Chloroplast Structure|open note]]",
			"x": 520,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "ps",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Photosystems\nAntenna pigments → reaction center → primary e⁻ acceptor; PSII P680, PSI P700\n\n[[Photosystems|open note]]",
			"x": 520,
			"y": 490,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "lrx",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Light reactions\nH₂O split; ETC; H⁺ gradient; makes O₂, ATP, NADPH\n\n[[Light Reactions|open note]]",
			"x": 520,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "z",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Z scheme\nElectron energy: two light-driven lifts, two downhill runs\n\n[[Z Scheme|open note]]",
			"x": 520,
			"y": 950,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "atp",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### ATP and NADPH\nEnergy carrier and electron carrier; redox\n\n[[ATP and NADPH|open note]]",
			"x": 520,
			"y": 1180,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "ov",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Photosynthesis overview\n6 CO₂ + 6 H₂O + light → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6 O₂\n\n[[Photosynthesis Overview|open note]]",
			"x": 1040,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "cal",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Calvin–Benson cycle\nFixation (RuBisCO) → reduction → regeneration; 6 CO₂ + 18 ATP + 12 NADPH = 1 glucose\n\n[[Calvin-Benson Cycle|open note]]",
			"x": 1040,
			"y": 490,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "carb",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Carbohydrates\nGlucose, maltose, sucrose, starch; dehydration synthesis and hydrolysis\n\n[[Carbohydrates and Glycosidic Bonds|open note]]",
			"x": 1040,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "iki",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Activity 8: IKI\nStarch helix traps iodine: blue-black\n\n[[Activity 8 - IKI Test for Starch|open note]]",
			"x": 1040,
			"y": 950,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "ben",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Activity 9: Benedict's\nReducing sugars: blue → orange when heated\n\n[[Activity 9 - Benedict Test for Reducing Sugars|open note]]",
			"x": 1040,
			"y": 1180,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "auto",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Autotrophs vs heterotrophs\nMake food vs. eat food; both respire\n\n[[Autotrophs vs Heterotrophs|open note]]",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "act6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Activities 6 and 11\nElodea, Cladophora, Spirogyra, Oscillatoria\n\n[[Activity 6 and 11 - Photosynthetic Autotrophs|open note]]",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 490,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "fc",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Food chains\nProducer → consumers; arrows follow the energy\n\n[[Food Chains and Trophic Levels|open note]]",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "pyr",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Energy pyramid\nAbout 10% passes up each trophic level\n\n[[Energy Pyramid and the 10 Percent Rule|open note]]",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 950,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "resp",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Glycolysis and respiration\nGlucose + O₂ → CO₂ + H₂O + ATP; the reverse of photosynthesis\n\n[[Glycolysis and Cellular Respiration|open note]]",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 1180,
			"width": 330,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "g_leaf",
			"type": "group",
